{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/955396-dreaminggod-s-new-homebrew-hub","id":955396,"title":"DreamingGod's (new) homebrew hub.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T20:56:43-07:00","id":955396,"title":"DreamingGod's (new) homebrew hub.","content":"So, using free time at work I have begun to slowly work again at my homebrew. As my first part I am rewriting my Salubri in the style of PenDragon's bloodlines-as-clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9xE2fn3u_o8bm_rNio1v84hfOpwu5O94_u_9rdytrU/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9xE2fn3u_o8bm_rNio1v84hfOpwu5O94_u_9rdytrU/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9xE2fn3u_o8bm_rNio1v84hfOpwu5O94_u_9rdytrU/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9xE2fn3u_o8bm_rNio1v84hfOpwu5O94_u_9rdytrU/edit?usp=drive_web </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This includes a more streamlined Valeren too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:08:51-07:00","id":956394,"title":"","content":"Comments on Valeren;<br /> <br /> The direction I weny with is a Discipline of soul manipulation. An extension of the Kindred's batural ability to devour souls. It is based largely off the Dragon Pearl KotE Discipline, but also Valeren. The specific paths are now Bloodline Gifts, anf Valeren is a Discipline any can learn. It is more common in the East, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:08:42-07:00","id":959223,"title":"","content":"Does a Valeren gain one of Rasa, Burning Touch, etc. for free or are they all 2xp?<br /> <br /> Where is says &quot;Healers take 7 - Humanity less Vitae from a victim if they are unwilling&quot;, this means that Kindred with lower Humanity are <i>more</i> affected by the curse? Except I would assume that higher Humanity Healers would be more disturbed by drinking from an unwilling victim. Perhaps remove the Humanity link and make it <i>Blood Potency + 1 </i>less Vitae? So the curse is stronger in those who have lived longer, regardless of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Third Eye sight seems quite powerful as it is free. I would activate it at the start of every scene! Perhaps it should come with a base roll, or even some disadvantages? If it appears as a physical eye in the forehead perhaps it could impact social rolls with Mortals or risk a Masquerade breach?<br /> <br /> The combo of the discipline and gifts do seem quite wide-ranging: from auspex-like insight to healing.<br /> <br /> Other than that I do like it. I might steal Ending the Watch as a Devotion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , it has great opportunities for dramatic choices with dying NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12208-verblet","name":"verblet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:41:41-07:00","id":960689,"title":"","content":"They gain Rasa for free, the others are 2 xp a piece.<br /> <br /> I may change the weakness, but it is currently the same as the Bane in VtR 2nd. <br /> <br /> Third Eye's Sight is currently supposed to open up the third eye, but I may make Valeren's third eye spiritual and make the Salubri's weakness give them a physical third eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}